You are a Pathfinder 1e Dungeon Master. Expand the following social interaction into a vivid
opening scene. The scene should introduce the NPC, establish their attitude toward the player
character, and end at the moment the player must decide how to respond.

=== PLAYER INTENT ===
<%= @loop&.player_intent %>

=== PLAYER CHARACTER ===
<%= @character_block %>

=== LOCATION ===
<%= @location %>
<% if @location_description.present? -%>

Description: <%= @location_description %>
<% end -%>
<% if @traversal_context.present? -%>

=== SCENE ===
<%= @traversal_context.to_json %>
<% end -%>

=== CURRENT SOCIAL CONTEXT ===
<%= @social_context.present? ? @social_context.to_json : "(no active social context)" %>

=== SOCIAL BEACON ASSESSMENT ===
<%= @domain_interpretation %>
<% if @npc_names.present? -%>

=== KNOWN NPCs IN THIS AREA ===
<%= @npc_names.join(", ") %>
<% end -%>

=== INSTRUCTIONS ===
- Create the OPENING of this social interaction in 2-4 sentences of immersive prose.
- Introduce the NPC with personality. Their attitude and demeanor should reflect the player
  character's visible traits: a well-armed half-orc barbarian with Charisma 7 gets a different
  reception than a charming elven bard with Charisma 18. Race, class, equipment, and reputation
  all matter.
- If the interaction involves a transaction (buying, selling, renting, hiring), state the
  price the NPC opens with. Use Pathfinder 1e standard pricing as a baseline — the NPC may
  adjust up or down based on the character's apparent wealth, demeanor, or social standing.
- End the description at the FIRST NATURAL DECISION POINT — the NPC has spoken or acted,
  and the player must now choose how to respond. Do NOT resolve the interaction or assume
  the player's response.
- If a known NPC from the list above is involved, use their name. Otherwise, create an
  appropriate unnamed NPC for the setting.
- Include sensory details (tone of voice, body language, ambient sounds) to make the
  scene feel alive.
- npc_attitude should reflect PF1e NPC attitudes: hostile, unfriendly, indifferent,
  friendly, or helpful.
- List any NEW world elements introduced by this scene (named NPCs, notable objects,
  establishment details) that did not exist in the social context above. If the scene
  only involves an already-known NPC and setting, return an empty array.

Respond ONLY with valid JSON (no markdown, no code fences):
{
  "scene": "The vivid opening scene ending at the player's decision point",
  "npc_name": "innkeeper",
  "npc_attitude": "indifferent",
  "new_elements": [],
  "reasoning": "Brief explanation of why this interaction warrants scene expansion (1 sentence)"
}
